# Active Directory User Administration Lab

## Overview

This lab was created in a Windows Server Active Directory environment to practice common user administration and help desk tasks in an enterprise domain environment.

The lab focuses on Active Directory administration rather than installation, including organizational structure, user management, security groups, and shared folder permissions.



# Objectives

- Create and organize Organizational Units (OUs)
- Create and manage Active Directory users
- Create and manage security groups
- Assign users to groups
- Configure shared folder permissions
- Simulate common help desk administration tasks



# Environment

- Windows Server
- Active Directory Domain Services
- Active Directory Users and Computers
- NTFS Permissions
- Windows File Sharing


# Organizational Unit Structure


Company
├── Users
│   ├── IT
│   ├── HR
│   └── Sales
│
├── Computers
├── Security Groups
└── Disabled Users




# Administrative Tasks Performed

## User Administration

- Created department users
- Reset passwords
- Disabled user accounts
- Organized users into departmental OUs

## Security Groups

Created groups including:
- IT-Staff
- HR-Staff
- Sales-Staff
- VPN-Users

## Shared Folder Permissions

Configured departmental shared folders with group-based permissions.

Examples:
- HR share
- IT share
- Sales share



# Skills Practiced

- Active Directory administration
- Organizational Unit management
- User onboarding/offboarding
- Security group administration
- NTFS permissions
- Shared folder management
- Windows Server administration
- Enterprise user management







